From dfdc6bc3ed78c38676fbcfb426e463dc593c39e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ye Li <ye.li@nxp.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Dec 2025 11:46:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] LFU-953-2 arm: dts: imx93w-evk: Configure CCM_CLKO1 pin to
 GPIO

CCM_CLKO1 default iomux setting 0 is used for output of CCM CLKO1 clock.
However on i.MX93W, it connects to IW610 boot config[3]. If it outputs clock,
the boot mode of IW610 may be wrong.
In u-boot, we have to configure CCM_CLKO1 to GPIO input and internal pull up
to resolve the problem. Since CCM_CLKO1 eventually will be used as SPI_INT
for IW610, the setting is aligned with SPI_INT.

Backported from NXP uboot-imx lf-6.18.20-2.0.0 commit dfdc6bc3ed78.
This fixes the intermittent IW610 SDIO init failure on i.MX93W EVK
(CMD5 responds but OCR ready bit never sets -> error -110) caused by
the CCM_CLKO1 clock output disturbing the IW610 boot-mode strap.

Signed-off-by: Ye Li <ye.li@nxp.com>
Reviewed-by: Peng Fan <peng.fan@nxp.com>
---
 arch/arm/dts/imx93w-evk-u-boot.dtsi | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/dts/imx93w-evk-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/imx93w-evk-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -5,6 +5,19 @@
 
 #include "imx93-11x11-evk-u-boot.dtsi"
 
+&iomuxc {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_hog>;
+
+	pinctrl_hog: hoggrp {
+		bootph-all;
+
+		fsl,pins = <
+			MX93_PAD_CCM_CLKO1__GPIO3_IO26			0x31e
+		>;
+	};
+};
+
 &pinctrl_lpi2c3_gpio {
        fsl,pins = <
                MX93_PAD_GPIO_IO00__GPIO2_IO00                  0x31e
